WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.733
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:16.076
Unit twenty: Mock Exam Review and Strategy. Today you will review all skills and plan the final weeks.

4
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:19.040
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.256
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:25.768
Mock exam.

7
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:28.992
Mock exam means a practice test.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:30.840
Do a mock exam.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.009
Your turn. Say: Mock exam.

10
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:38.413
Mock exam.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.174
Weakness.

12
00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:43.392
Weakness means a point that needs work.

13
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:45.193
Find your weakness.

14
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:48.482
Your turn. Say: Weakness.

15
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.276
Weakness.

16
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:53.867
Strength.

17
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:56.883
Strength means a point you do well.

18
00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:58.914
Grammar is my strength.

19
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:01.844
Your turn. Say: Strength.

20
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.678
Strength.

21
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.476
Timetable.

22
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:11.238
Timetable means a study plan with times.

23
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.234
Make a timetable.

24
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.328
Your turn. Say: Timetable.

25
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.191
Timetable.

26
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:21.719
Review.

27
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:24.530
Review means to study again.

28
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.524
Review your notes.

29
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:30.013
Your turn. Say: Review.

30
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:33.821
Review.

31
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:35.666
Past paper.

32
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.963
Past paper means an old exam.

33
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.934
Do a past paper.

34
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:44.272
Your turn. Say: Past paper.

35
00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.320
Past paper.

36
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.061
Feedback.

37
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.595
Feedback means comments to help you improve.

38
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:55.591
Ask for feedback.

39
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:58.464
Your turn. Say: Feedback.

40
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.139
Feedback.

41
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:03.954
Achieve.

42
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.706
Achieve means to reach a goal.

43
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:08.782
I will achieve my goal.

44
00:02:09.383 --> 00:02:12.256
Your turn. Say: Achieve.

45
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.113
Achieve.

46
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.284
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.359
Visal, how do I use a mock exam?

48
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:35.020
Do it in exam conditions with a time limit. Then mark it carefully and list your mistakes by topic, such as tenses, articles or reading inference.

49
00:02:36.117 --> 00:02:37.989
How do I plan the last weeks?

50
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:49.842
Make a timetable. Spend more time on weaknesses, but keep reviewing your strengths. Do one past paper each week and ask your teacher for feedback.

51
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:52.427
What about the final night?

52
00:02:53.517 --> 00:03:05.225
Review a short summary of key rules, pack your pens and ID, and sleep well. On the exam day, read every instruction and manage your time.

53
00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.157
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.017 --> 00:03:12.700
Grammar focus: review, practise, improve.

55
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.187
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:17.138
I will review my mistakes every weekend.

57
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.282
I will do one past paper each week.

58
00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:28.599
Use mock exams to find weaknesses, make a timetable, practise with past papers and ask for feedback. Stay calm and organised.

59
00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.711
Be careful! Don't say: I study only my strengths.

60
00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.212
Say: I also study my weaknesses.

61
00:03:37.512 --> 00:03:38.896
Work on weak points.

62
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.770
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:44.788
The Last Weeks.

64
00:03:45.088 --> 00:03:48.144
Sreyleak does a mock exam on Saturday.

65
00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.760
She marks it and lists her mistakes by topic.

66
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.370
She finds that her weakness is reported speech.

67
00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.307
She makes a timetable and practises it every day.

68
00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.114
She is ready to achieve her goal.

69
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.376
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.217 --> 00:04:10.425
A mock exam is a blank test.

71
00:04:10.725 --> 00:04:13.961
A, real. B, lost. C, practice.

72
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.407
The answer is C: practice.

73
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.782
A weakness is a point that needs blank.

74
00:04:23.082 --> 00:04:26.271
A, work. B, money. C, music.

75
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:31.752
The answer is A: work.

76
00:04:32.917 --> 00:04:35.032
Sreyleak's weakness is blank.

77
00:04:35.332 --> 00:04:39.880
A, drawing. B, reported speech. C, maths.

78
00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:45.944
The answer is B: reported speech.

79
00:04:47.083 --> 00:04:49.060
A timetable helps you blank.

80
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.642
A, forget. B, sleep. C, plan.

81
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.223
The answer is C: plan.

82
00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:01.360
Past papers are blank exams.

83
00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.616
A, old. B, new. C, fake.

84
00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.853
The answer is A: old.

85
00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:14.079
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.917 --> 00:05:16.394
What is your study plan?

87
00:05:25.183 --> 00:05:26.660
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:38.009
I will do one past paper every week and review my mistakes. I will spend more time on my weak points. I will ask my teacher for feedback and sleep well before the exam.

89
00:05:38.309 --> 00:05:40.332
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:41.217 --> 00:05:45.599
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and review, practise, improve.

91
00:05:45.899 --> 00:05:50.374
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:05:50.674 --> 00:05:58.228
Congratulations! You have finished Online Cambodia Grade twelve English. See you in Online more new courses soon!

93
00:05:58.528 --> 00:06:01.192
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

